From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rahanahu <rahanahu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vasio: do not advertise a participant whose connection is
 closed

When a participant's connection to the registry ends, the stream closes
its socket at once, but the registry learns of it later: OnShutdown() is
posted to the I/O context, and until OnPeerShutdown() runs the
participant stays in _connectedParticipants. If the announcement of a
joining participant is handled in between, SendKnownParticipants() asks
TransformAcceptorUris() for the remote address of the closed socket,
which throws std::system_error ("remote_endpoint: Bad file descriptor").
ReceiveParticipantAnnouncement() catches only SilKitError, so the
exception ends up in the I/O worker ("SilKit-IOWorker: Something went
wrong"), the joining participant gets neither the known participants nor
a reply, and its CreateParticipant() fails after ConnectTimeoutSeconds
with "Timeout during connection handshake with the SIL Kit Registry".

Leave such a participant out of the known participants: nobody can
connect to it anymore.
---
 SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioRegistry.cpp | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioRegistry.cpp b/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioRegistry.cpp
index a7bc41d2..46e2ce1e 100644
--- a/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioRegistry.cpp
+++ b/SilKit/source/core/vasio/VAsioRegistry.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 
 #include "core/internal/traits/SilKitServiceConfigTraits.hpp"
 
+#include <system_error>
+
 
 namespace Log = SilKit::Services::Logging;
 
@@ -299,7 +301,22 @@ void VAsioRegistry::SendKnownParticipants(IVAsioPeer* peer, const std::string& s
             continue;
 
         auto peerInfo = connectedParticipant.peerInfo;
-        peerInfo.acceptorUris = TransformAcceptorUris(GetLoggerInternal(), connectedParticipant.peer, peer);
+        try
+        {
+            peerInfo.acceptorUris = TransformAcceptorUris(GetLoggerInternal(), connectedParticipant.peer, peer);
+        }
+        catch (const std::system_error& error)
+        {
+            // The connection to the advertised participant is closed already, but its shutdown has not been
+            // processed yet (it is still in the list): the addresses of its socket cannot be read anymore.
+            // Nobody can connect to it, so it is not a known participant.
+            GetLoggerInternal()
+                ->MakeMessage(Log::Level::Debug, TopicOf(*this))
+                .SetMessage("Not advertising participant '{}' to '{}', its connection is closed: {}", pPair.first,
+                            peer->GetInfo().participantName, error.what())
+                .Dispatch();
+            continue;
+        }
 
         knownParticipantsMsg.peerInfos.push_back(peerInfo);
     }
